#: src/dippi.blp:218
msgid ""
"For LoDPI, a DPI range of <b>90–150 is ideal for desktops</b> while <b>124–"
"156 is ideal for laptops</b>.\n"
"\n"
"For HiDPI, <b>180–300 is ideal for desktops</b> while <b>248–312 is ideal "
"for laptops</b>."
msgstr ""

#: src/dippi.blp:254
msgid "Very Low DPI"
msgstr "PPP muy bajos"

#: src/dippi.blp:267
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Text and UI are likely to be too big for typical viewing distances. <b>Avoid "
"if possible.</b>"
msgstr ""
"Es probable que el texto y la interfaz resulten demasiado grandes a "
"distancias de visión habituales. Evítela en lo posible."

#: src/dippi.blp:303
msgid "Fairly Low DPI"
msgstr "PPP relativamente escasos"

#: src/dippi.blp:316
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Text and UI might be too big for typical viewing distances, but it's "
"<b>largely up to user preference</b> and physical distance from the display."
msgstr ""
"El texto y la interfaz podrían ser demasiado grandes a distancias de visión "
"habituales, pero depende en gran medida de la preferencia del usuario y de "
"la distancia física con la pantalla."

#: src/dippi.blp:352
msgid "Ideal for LoDPI"
msgstr "Ideal para resolución baja"

#: src/dippi.blp:365
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Not HiDPI, but <b>a nice sweet spot</b>. Text and UI should be legible at "
"typical viewing distances."
msgstr ""
"No es de alta resolución, mas es un punto de equilibrio óptimo. El texto y "
"la interfaz serán legibles a distancias de visión habituales."

#: src/dippi.blp:401 src/dippi.blp:499 src/dippi.blp:548
msgid "Potentially Problematic"
msgstr "Potencialmente problemática"

#: src/dippi.blp:414
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Relatively high resolution, but not quite HiDPI. Text and UI <b>may be too "
"small by default</b>, but forcing HiDPI would make them appear too large. "
"The experience may be slightly improved by increasing the text size."
msgstr ""
"La resolución es relativamente elevada sin ser «de alta resolución». Es "
"probable que el texto y la interfaz resulten muy pequeños de manera "
"predeterminada, y forzar una escala superior los agrandaría demasiado. Si "
"aumenta el tamaño del texto, la experiencia puede mejorar un poco."

#: src/dippi.blp:450
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tweak for HiDPI"
msgstr "Ideal para resolución alta"

#: src/dippi.blp:463
msgid ""
"This display may default to loDPI on some desktops, which could result in "
"too-small text and UI. However, it <b>may be usable with HiDPI by manually "
"enabling 2× scaling</b>. Further adjustments can be made by decreasing the "
"text size."
msgstr ""

#: src/dippi.blp:512
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This display is in a very tricky range and is <b>not likely to work well</b> "
"with integer scaling out of the box."
msgstr ""
"Esta pantalla se encuentra en un intervalo muy intricado y podría no "
"funcionar adecuadamente con el ajuste de escala por enteros a la primera "
"instalación."

#: src/dippi.blp:561
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"HiDPI by default, but <b>text and UI may appear too large</b>. Turning off "
"HiDPI and increasing the text size might help."
msgstr ""
"Alta resolución de manera predeterminada, pero el texto y la interfaz pueden "
"mostrarse demasiado grandes. Considere desactivar el modo de alta resolución "
"y aumentar el tamaño del texto."

#: src/dippi.blp:597
msgid "Ideal for HiDPI"
msgstr "Ideal para resolución alta"

#: src/dippi.blp:610
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Crisp HiDPI text and UI along with a readable size at typical viewing "
"distances. <b>This is the jackpot.</b>"
msgstr ""
"El texto y la interfaz de alta resolución se mostrarán nítidos a distancias "
"de visión habituales. Este es el premio mayor."

#: src/dippi.blp:646
msgid "Fairly High for HiDPI"
msgstr "Bastante elevada para resolución alta"

#: src/dippi.blp:659
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Text and UI are likely to appear <b>too small for typical viewing distances</"
"b>. Increasing the text size may help."
msgstr ""
"Es probable que el texto y la interfaz resulten demasiado pequeños a "
"distancias de visión habituales. Considere aumentar el tamaño del texto."

#: src/dippi.blp:708
#, fuzzy
msgid "Text and UI will appear <b>too small for typical viewing distances</b>."
